              = succeed "," do
                %em Finiteness of type II superstring amplitudes
          %p argues finiteness of the superstring amplitudes at each order.
          %p Also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"}> Eric D'Hoker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Momentum Analyticity and Finiteness of the 1-Loop Superstring Amplitude
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9302003"} arXiv:hep-th/9302003
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"}> Eric D'Hoker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Box Graph In Superstring Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9410152"} arXiv:hep-th/9410152
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"}> Eric D'Hoker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em Dispersion Relations in String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9404128"} arXiv:hep-th/9404128
          %p
            Arguments for the finiteness of superstring scattering amplitudes to all loop order based on the
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berkovits+superstring"} Berkovits superstring
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multiloop Amplitudes and Vanishing Theorems using the Pure Spinor Formalism for the Superstring
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406055"} arXiv:hep-th/0406055
          %p
            (In footnote 2 this article claims that the claimed proofs of the same statement by G.S Danilov in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9801013"} hep-th/9801013
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312177"} hep-th/0312177
            are not in fact proofs.)
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-loop"} 2-loop
            amplitudes from holomorphy arguments:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Notes On Holomorphic String And Superstring Theory Measures Of Low Genus
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.3621"}> arXiv:1306.3621
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              ,
              %em Supersymmetry Restoration in Superstring Perturbation Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1508.02481"}> arXiv:1508.02481
              )
          %h3#graviton_scattering Graviton scattering
          %p
            Computation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
            scattering amplitudes (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+gravity"}> perturbative quantum gravity
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravitational Scattering Amplitudes and Closed String Field Theory in the Proper-Time Gauge
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1051/epjconf/201816807004"} doi:10.1051/epjconf/201816807004
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
                ,
                %em Four-Graviton Scattering and String Path Integral in the Proper-time gauge
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.02702"}> arXiv:1806.02702
                )
          %h3#ReferencesViaAdSCFT Via AdS/CFT
          %p
            Discussion via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            beyond the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SCFT"} SCFT
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+limit"} planar limit
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+bootstrap"} conformal bootstrap
          %ul
            %li#ABP18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alday"}> Luis Alday
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agnese+Bissi"} Agnese Bissi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Perlmutter"} Eric Perlmutter
              = succeed "," do
                %em Genus-One String Amplitudes from Conformal Field Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.10670"} arXiv:1809.10670
          %h3#more More
          %p
            On point-particle limit via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tropical+geometry"} tropical geometry
          %ul
            %li
              Piotr Tourkine,
              %em Tropical Amplitudes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.3551"}> arXiv:1309.3551
              )
          %p Scattering amplitudes of highly excited strings:
          %ul
            %li
              Dimitri P. Skliros, Edmund J. Copeland, Paul M. Saffin,
              %em Highly Excited Strings I: Generating Function
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.06498"}> arxiv:1611.06498
              )
